{# The painter's light/dark switch, applied to every page before it paints.

   The painter remembers a choice under `neo-cucumber-theme` and marks the
   root `data-theme`; every token on the site and in the painter honours that
   ahead of the system setting, so the painter's switch is the site's switch
   too. It has to run here, in the head, rather than wait for the painter to
   mount: a page that paints first and then turns dark flashes. Boosted
   navigation keeps the root element, so the mark survives it. #}
<script>
  try {
    var theme = localStorage.getItem("neo-cucumber-theme");
    if (theme === "light" || theme === "dark") {
      document.documentElement.setAttribute("data-theme", theme);
    }
  } catch (error) {
    // Storage refused: the system setting decides, as it does by default.
  }
</script>
